<title>JAPAN: BOJ injects 300 bln yen into market -- traders.</title>
<headline>BOJ injects 300 bln yen into market -- traders.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Japan (BOJ) injected a net 300 billion yen into the money market on Wednesday, money traders said.  </p>
<p>The injection resulted in a market surplus of about 300 billion yen for the day, traders said.</p>
<p>The operation was more accommodative than in previous days, they said. The BOJ left a market surplus of some 200 billion yen on Monday and on Tuesday.</p>
</text>
